<DocumentFragment>
  <div
    class="flex justify-between"
  >
    <h2
      class="font-(family-name:--title-fonts) font-bold text-2xl"
    >
      How to Play
    </h2>
    <button
      class="w-4 cursor-pointer -mt-4"
      type="button"
    >
      <svg
        viewBox="0 0 640 640"
        xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
      >
        <path
          d="M183.1 137.4C170.6 124.9 150.3 124.9 137.8 137.4C125.3 149.9 125.3 170.2 137.8 182.7L275.2 320L137.9 457.4C125.4 469.9 125.4 490.2 137.9 502.7C150.4 515.2 170.7 515.2 183.2 502.7L320.5 365.3L457.9 502.6C470.4 515.1 490.7 515.1 503.2 502.6C515.7 490.1 515.7 469.8 503.2 457.3L365.8 320L503.1 182.6C515.6 170.1 515.6 149.8 503.1 137.3C490.6 124.8 470.3 124.8 457.8 137.3L320.5 274.7L183.1 137.4z"
          fill="rgb(255, 255, 255)"
        />
      </svg>
    </button>
  </div>
  <p
    class="font-(family-name:--title-fonts) mb-2"
  >
    Connect the start and end words using similar words.
  </p>
  <ul
    class="font-(family-name:--standard-fonts) pl-2"
  >
    <li>
      • Change 
      <span
        class="font-extrabold"
      >
        exactly one
      </span>
       letter between each guess,
      <br />
      indicated by the 
      <span
        class="text-pink-bright"
      >
        pink
      </span>
       tiles.
    </li>
    <li>
      • Each guess must be a valid 5-letter word.
    </li>
    <li
      class="sm:hidden"
    >
      • Guesses can be selected by pressing on them or using Enter/Backspace on the keyboard.
    </li>
    <li
      class="hidden sm:list-item"
    >
      • Guesses can be selected using the mouse, the arrow keys or Enter/Backspace.
    </li>
    <li>
      • Use the + and - buttons at the top of the page to add and remove guesses.
    </li>
    <li>
      • Press Enter on the final guess to submit.
    </li>
    <li>
      • Don't worry, you can keep trying if the submission isn't valid!
    </li>
  </ul>
</DocumentFragment>